@architect-ingestion-v2 @feat-rag-08
Feature: Architect ingestion v2 — llama-swap migration and docling-direct path
  As an operator maintaining the architect's knowledge index
  I want ingestion and retrieval-time embeddings to flow through the fleet-canonical llama-swap endpoint, and to be able to add new architecture books from docling-produced markdown without re-running the dataset factory
  So that the architect honours the fleet-wide llama-swap-only policy and the corpus can be refreshed on demand

  Background:
    Given llama-swap is reachable on the GB10 host and serves the configured embedding model
    And the architect-knowledge-v1 collection already holds 768-dimension vectors
    And ingestion is invoked from the GB10 host where the persistence directory lives

