  # GROUP A: Key Examples
  # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  # Why: Core migration path — re-running ingestion against the migrated endpoint must keep the existing collection queryable so retrieval traffic continues without a re-build.
  @task:TASK-AIV2-002
  @key-example @smoke
  Scenario: Re-ingesting the existing knowledge.jsonl through llama-swap preserves vector parity
    Given the architect-knowledge-v1 collection was previously populated via the fleet-canonical embedding model
    When the operator re-runs the ingestion script with the llama-swap embedding endpoint configured
    Then ingestion should complete without raising a collection identity mismatch
    And every previously-ingested row should remain queryable
    And new vectors should be 768-dimensional and produced by the same embedding model

  # Why: Core docling-direct path — proves a new architecture book can land without going through the dataset factory.
  @task:TASK-AIV2-003
  @key-example @smoke
  Scenario: Ingesting a docling-produced markdown architecture book lands chunks in the collection
    # [ASSUMPTION: confidence=medium] Docling-markdown source files live under data/rag_index/markdown/ alongside the gitignored knowledge.jsonl
    # [ASSUMPTION: confidence=low] Per-file YAML frontmatter supplies the seven canonical metadata keys (dimension, source_books, topic, layer, source, turns, type)
    # [ASSUMPTION: confidence=medium] CLI shape is --source jsonl|markdown with auto-detection by file extension when omitted
    Given a docling-produced markdown file for a newly-added architecture book
    And the file has been verified to contain no residual layout-token artefacts
    When the operator runs the ingestion script in markdown mode against that file
    Then the file should be chunked into paragraph-level extracts
    And each extract should be embedded via llama-swap and persisted into the architect-knowledge collection
    And the run summary should report the new chunks under the docling-direct origin

  # Why: Retrieval-time embeddings must also flow through llama-swap, not Ollama — otherwise the migration is half-done and queries still hit the forbidden endpoint.
  @task:TASK-AIV2-006
  @key-example @smoke
  Scenario: The architect retrieval tool embeds queries via llama-swap at runtime
    Given the architect Player issues a retrieval query against the knowledge index
    When the retrieval tool generates an embedding for the query
    Then the embedding request should be sent to the llama-swap embedding endpoint
    And no request should be sent to the Ollama embeddings endpoint

  # Why: End-to-end smoke proves migration plus docling-direct co-exist on the FEAT-RAG-03 retrieval path with citations rendered correctly.
  @task:TASK-AIV2-006
  @key-example
  Scenario: A retrieval query returns cited extracts drawn from both JSONL- and docling-sourced rows
    Given the collection contains rows ingested from both knowledge.jsonl and a docling-produced markdown file
    When the operator submits a smoke-test retrieval query that matches both sources
    Then the result list should contain at least one extract from the JSONL-sourced rows
    And the result list should contain at least one extract from the docling-sourced rows
    And every extract should be prefixed with its [source_book: topic] citation line

